      "difficulty_reason": "The author combines a weighted matrix-forest comparison with path-tree/matching-polynomial bounds, controls the excess through cycle-indexed loss terms, and matches the two exponential decay constants termwise to obtain the conjectured degree-dependent sharp exponential base. Complete local determinant, expansion, path-tree and analytic lemmas are retained. The prior cubic case and high-girth sharpness are explicitly attributed; the quantitative cycle correction is part of the same bound, not a second count.",
